nct margins or right-sided pathology, regardless of how well they fit a preferred diagnosis. CRITICAL ADDITION 4: When evaluating syndromic diagnoses involving multiple organ systems (e.g., Kartagener's syndrome), ensure all required components are visually verified. If a prominent anatomical variant (e.g., situs inversus/dextrocardia) is identified, do not stop there; actively search for the associated parenchymal pathology (e.g., bronchiectasis) which may be subtle or missed by classifiers. Prioritize the option that describes the specific lung pathology required by the syndrome over the option describing only the positional anomaly, unless the lung pathology is definitively absent."
